From 1546bd7dc470e5799a7662711f78db14b53517a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:04:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 22/51] fix: lost admit races no longer orphan or double-own
 coherence records; reclaim never frees an unlocked record

Attempt 12 (G-B v2.12, f1-art64) hung with writer_owner_mismatch > 0: a key's
record carried another key's BlockId. Three upstream defects:

- CheckPutArrayWmeta(key, cn, NUMA_MEM, -1) (RO admit losing to an existing
  slot) set the key's wmeta to -1 even when the key was RW: the record was
  dropped without a free and without the RO switch's deallocation event.
  Now an RW key is left unchanged (None); only an already-RO key is idempotent.
- Admit/AdmitWrite treated GCD_SLOT_UPDATE_FAILED ("slot exists") as a failed
  install and freed the record, although the op had installed it on the RO
  key. The key then pointed at a free record that the next allocation gave to
  another key. Now the record is kept (WSeqEnd); only the cache node is freed.
- artifact64 reclaim: when the RO switch of the victim's BlockId answered a
  different record, upstream freed that record without holding its lock
  (stealing a writer's lock or leaking it) and left the victim locked forever.
  SharedMetadata::FinishReclaim now unlocks the victim and frees the other
  record only after locking it. rev64/packed4 behaviour is unchanged.

Diag counters reclaim_victim_mismatch and admit_record_installed in DiagSummary.
Rust test admit_on_existing_slot_never_demotes_and_reports_installed_record.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
